prompt:
You are assisting with business process modelling. List the steps of the business process described below.

INSTRUCTIONS
- A step is one thing that an actor does in the process. Use only what the description states. Do not add steps that the description does not state.
- Give every step: step_id (S1, S2, ... in the order of the description), actor (who does it), activity (what is done, in a few words), data_or_object (the data, document or object the step handles; empty string if none) and quote.
- quote: copy the words of the description that state the step, word for word. Do not change, shorten in the middle or rephrase the words.
- Answer with one JSON object that follows the JSON schema below. Output only the JSON, with no other text.

EXAMPLE (made up, for the format only)
Description: "The customer chooses a product. The shop sends the product and an invoice."
Answer: {"steps": [{"step_id": "S1", "actor": "customer", "activity": "choose a product", "data_or_object": "product", "quote": "The customer chooses a product"}, {"step_id": "S2", "actor": "shop", "activity": "send the product and an invoice", "data_or_object": "product, invoice", "quote": "The shop sends the product and an invoice"}]}

JSON SCHEMA
{
  "$defs": {
    "Step": {
      "properties": {
        "step_id": {
          "description": "S1, S2, ... in the order of the description",
          "title": "Step Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "actor": {
          "description": "Who does the step",
          "title": "Actor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "activity": {
          "description": "What is done, in a few words",
          "title": "Activity",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "data_or_object": {
          "description": "The data, document or object the step handles; empty string if none",
          "title": "Data Or Object",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "quote": {
          "description": "Exact words copied from the process description that state the step",
          "title": "Quote",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "step_id",
        "actor",
        "activity",
        "data_or_object",
        "quote"
      ],
      "title": "Step",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "steps": {
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/Step"
      },
      "title": "Steps",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "steps"
  ],
  "title": "StepsOutput",
  "type": "object"
}

PROCESS DESCRIPTION
The process begins when a customer files a complaint about a product or service.
Customer service logs the complaint and assigns it to the relevant department for investigation.
After reviewing the details, the team determines whether the complaint is valid and whether a refund is justified and notifies the customer with the decision.
If a refund is approved, the financial team processes the reimbursement.
The complaint is marked as resolved once the customer receives the refund or directly after notifying the customer in case the refund was rejected.
After resolving the case, customers can provide feedback on their satisfaction.
Most complaints come from private persons whose kitchen appliance stopped working a few months after purchase. These customers usually ask for the appliance to be fixed or swapped for a new one.

